      "card_ref": "EV-PHY-11-MIP-08-015",
      "independent_solution": [
        "Launch and landing on the floor, no drag, g = 9.8 m/s^2. H = (v0 sin(theta))^2/(2g); at 45 deg H = 1600 x 0.5/19.6 = 40.8 m > 25 m, so the ceiling limits the angle.",
        "Range increases with theta up to 45 deg, so the best throw just grazes 25 m: (v0 sin(theta))^2 = 2 x 9.8 x 25 = 490 -> sin(theta) = 22.14/40 = 0.553 -> theta = 33.6 deg.",
        "R = v0^2 sin(2 theta)/g = 1600 x sin(67.2 deg)/9.8 = 1600 x 0.922/9.8 = 150.5 m."
      ],
      "independent_answer": "150.5 m",
      "official_answer": "150.5 m",
      "agrees": true,
      "numeric_check": "40**2*sin(2*asin(sqrt(2*9.8*25)/40))/9.8"
    },
    {
      "card_ref": "EV-PHY-11-MIP-08-017",
      "independent_solution": [
        "Maximum horizontal distance is at 45 deg: R_m = v0^2/g = 100 m, so v0^2 = 100 g.",
        "Greatest height for the same speed is a vertical throw: h = v0^2/(2g) = 100 g/(2g) = 50 m."
      ],
      "independent_answer": "50 m",
      "official_answer": "50 m",
      "agrees": true,
      "numeric_check": "100/2"
    },
    {
      "card_ref": "EV-PHY-11-MIP-08-019",
      "independent_solution": [
        "R = v0^2 sin(2 theta)/g; same v0 so R is proportional to sin(2 theta).",
        "R(45)/R(15) = sin 90 / sin 30 = 1/0.5 = 2 -> R(45) = 100 m: option (c)."
      ],
      "independent_answer": "(c) 100 m",
      "official_answer": "(c), 100 m",
      "agrees": true,
      "numeric_check": "50*sin(radians(90))/sin(radians(30))"
    }
